<main id="main">

<div class="hero">
  <h1>Backtest Engine Core</h1>
  <p class="subtitle">Orchestrator of Historical Simulation</p>
  <p>The central loop that replays every trading day, feeding market data through the agent ensemble and tracking portfolio evolution</p>
  <div style="margin-top:.8rem">
    <span class="badge blue">engine.py</span>
    <span class="badge green">~320 LOC</span>
    <span class="badge yellow">Orchestrator</span>
  </div>
</div>

<nav class="toc" id="toc"></nav>

<!-- ============================================================ -->
<div class="intro-box">
  <h3>🔍 What is this?</h3>
  <p>The <code>BacktestEngine</code> is the orchestrator of the entire historical simulation. It takes a date range, a set of stock tickers, and an initial capital amount, then replays every trading day through the full AI agent ensemble — the same ensemble used in live mode. It prefetches a year of market data, initializes a virtual portfolio, iterates day by day, executes trades, computes performance metrics, and produces a rich terminal output.</p>
  <div class="analogy">
    <strong>🎯 Analogy:</strong> Think of the BacktestEngine as a <strong>time machine for trading</strong>. Imagine you could rewind to January 1st, erase your memory of future prices, and hand your AI agents a fresh newspaper each morning. They read the news, check the financials, debate, and decide what to trade — then you advance the clock by one day and repeat. The time machine faithfully records every decision, every profit, and every loss. At the end, you step out and compare your AI's track record against what the S&amp;P 500 did over the same period.
  </div>
  <p>The engine itself is deliberately "dumb" about trading strategy — it delegates all intelligence to the agent ensemble via <code>run_hedge_fund()</code>. Its job is purely orchestration: getting the right data to the right place at the right time, and keeping meticulous books.</p>
</div>

<!-- ============================================================ -->
<h2 id="architecture">Architecture — Engine Internals</h2>

<div class="diagram-container">
<pre class="mermaid">
flowchart TD
    subgraph BacktestEngine
        INIT["__init__(config)"] --> PREFETCH["_prefetch_data()"]
        PREFETCH --> LOOP["run_backtest()"]
        LOOP --> |"for each bday"| DAY["_process_day(date)"]
        DAY --> SLICE["_slice_data(date)"]
        SLICE --> CTRL["AgentController\n.run_day()"]
        CTRL --> RHF["run_hedge_fund()"]
        RHF --> DECISIONS["trade_decisions[]"]
        DECISIONS --> EXEC["TradeExecutor\n.execute_all()"]
        EXEC --> VALIDATE["_validate_trade()"]
        VALIDATE --> APPLY["Portfolio\n.update_position()"]
        APPLY --> MTM["Valuation\n.mark_to_market()"]
        MTM --> METRICS["MetricsCalc\n.update()"]
        METRICS --> OUTPUT["OutputFormatter\n.render_day()"]
    end
    OUTPUT --> TERM["Terminal Display"]
    LOOP --> |"after loop"| SUMMARY["_generate_summary()"]
    SUMMARY --> FINAL["Final Report"]
</pre>
</div>

<p>The engine is structured as a <strong>three-phase pipeline</strong>:</p>
<ol>
  <li><strong>Initialization</strong> — config parsing, portfolio creation, and data prefetching</li>
  <li><strong>Daily Loop</strong> — the core iteration that processes each business day sequentially</li>
  <li><strong>Summary</strong> — post-loop aggregation, metric finalization, and report generation</li>
</ol>

<!-- ============================================================ -->
